---
/**
 * Privacy policy.
 *
 * TODO (BLOCKER — see docs/PROGRESS.md § B-6): this is a structural placeholder,
 * NOT legal advice and NOT launch-ready. It must be reviewed and completed by
 * someone qualified before the site goes live, particularly the controller
 * identity, retention periods, legal bases, and the supervisory authority.
 */
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Prose from '@/components/ui/Prose.astro'
import { SITE } from '@/config/site'

const updated = '26 August 2026'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How WildHands Studio collects, uses and stores personal data."
>
  <div class="wh-container pt-28 pb-16 md:pt-36 md:pb-24">
    <div class="max-w-[65ch]">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight md:text-5xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <div
        class="mt-8 rounded-xl border border-[color:var(--destructive)]/40 bg-[color:var(--destructive)]/5 p-5"
      >
        <p class="text-sm">
          <strong>Placeholder document.</strong> This policy is a structural draft only. It has not been
          reviewed by a qualified adviser and must be completed before launch.
        </p>
      </div>

      <Prose class="mt-10">
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          {SITE.legalName} operates this website. TODO: add the registered company name, company number,
          registered address, and the identity of the data controller.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>We collect personal data in three situations:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>When you contact us.</strong> Your name, email address, optional phone number, and
            whatever you write in the message.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>When you apply to work with us.</strong> Your name, contact details, professional
            profile links, your CV, and your answers to the application questions.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>When you accept analytics cookies.</strong> Anonymised usage data about which pages
            you visited. Analytics do not load unless you accept them.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
        <p>
          To reply to your enquiry, to assess your application, and to understand which parts of the
          site are useful. TODO: state the lawful basis for each purpose.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>TODO: specify retention periods for enquiries, applications, and analytics data.</p>

        <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
        <p>
          Form submissions are delivered by email through Resend, our email provider. Analytics,
          when you accept them, are processed by PostHog. TODO: confirm the full processor list,
          their locations, and the transfer mechanism for any processing outside the UK and EEA.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          The site sets no cookies until you make a choice in the consent banner. If you accept
          analytics, PostHog stores an identifier in your browser so repeat visits are not counted
          as new people. Declining leaves analytics switched off entirely.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us for a copy of your data, ask us to correct or delete it, or object to how
          we use it. TODO: name the supervisory authority and add the complaints route.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For anything about this policy, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
        </p>
      </Prose>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
